# Shell Rules

## Default shell: bash. Always.

Use bash for everything. Only use PowerShell when bash literally cannot do the task (see exceptions below).

When you reach for `Select-String`, `Get-ChildItem -Filter`, or any PowerShell pipeline — stop. Use bash instead.


## Bash path

Your bash binary: `{{BASH_PATH}}`

If `shell: "bash"` hangs or resolves to WSL, use the full path above instead:
`& "{{BASH_PATH}}" -c "your command"`

## How to use bash

In exec_command, pass `shell: "bash"`. That's it.

If `shell: "bash"` is not available, use `bash -c "your command"` from PowerShell.

## Bash tools

grep, sed, awk, find, xargs, make, patch, diff, tar, gzip, bzip2, xz, curl, wget, ssh, scp, vim, nano, less, which, tree, sort, uniq, wc, head, tail, cut, tr, tee, date, sleep

## When to use PowerShell (rare)

Only for these:
- Windows registry (`Get-ItemProperty`, `Set-ItemProperty`)
- Windows services (`Get-Service`, `Start-Service`)
- Windows processes (`Get-Process`, `Stop-Process`)
- .NET objects (`[System.IO.File]`, etc.)
- Windows Installer / MSI operations
- UnrealBuildTool / UE build scripts that require PowerShell

Everything else → bash.

## Mapping: PowerShell → bash

| Instead of | Use |
|------------|-----|
| `Select-String -Pattern "x"` | `grep "x"` |
| `Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Filter "*.py"` | `find . -name "*.py"` |
| `Get-ChildItem -Recurse \| Select-String "x"` | `grep -rn "x" .` |
| `ForEach-Object { $_ -replace "a","b" }` | `sed 's/a/b/g'` |
| `Measure-Object -Line` | `wc -l` |
| `Group-Object` | `sort \| uniq -c` |
| `Sort-Object -Descending` | `sort -r` |
| `Where-Object { ... }` | `grep -v` or `awk` |
| `Get-Content file \| Measure-Object` | `wc -l file` |
| `Copy-Item -Recurse` | `cp -r` |
| `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force` | `rm -rf` |
| `New-Item -ItemType Directory` | `mkdir -p` |
| `Get-Content` | `cat` or `less` |
| `Set-Content` | `echo "..." > file` |
| `Test-Path` | `test -f` or `test -d` |
| `Join-Path` | `$dir/$file` |

## Examples

Counting lines of code:
```bash
find src/ \( -name "*.py" -o -name "*.js" \) -exec cat {} + | wc -l
```

Searching for a pattern:
```bash
grep -rn "TODO" src/ --include="*.py"
```

Replacing text in files:
```bash
find src/ -name "*.py" -exec sed -i 's/old_func/new_func/g' {} +
```

## Encoding

UTF-8 everywhere. Never use GBK.


